  "method_note": "The SciTech 2026 online program (ATIV planner, id AIAASCITECH26) is offline ('Planner is currently unavailable') and the 2025 planner likewise; ARC is behind bot protection. Counted papers per AIAA technical discipline from the 65 discipline proceedings volumes 'Papers Presented at the AIAA SCITECH 2026 Forum' (Curran/proceedings.com IDs 85118-85182), counting table-of-contents entries: 2842 papers total (AIAA states ~3,000 presentations). Each discipline mapped to at most 2 keywords. Terrestrial Energy (28 papers) has no taxonomy match and was excluded, so weights are over 2814 papers. Keywords below 0.02 omitted (weights sum ~0.91). Fluid-dynamics-heavy disciplines dominate; AIAA GNC and Intelligent Systems volumes mix aircraft and spacecraft topics (split 50/50). deployable-structures added 2026-10-16: paper titles in the same 2026 discipline TOCs were screened for deployable booms/masts/trusses, deployable antennas/reflectors, membrane/inflatable, origami/kirigami, solar-sail hardware and deployment mechanisms; 26 space-structures papers were moved out of their discipline's keywords (22 Spacecraft Structures papers split 11/11 from structures and space-systems; 2 Structures and 1 Adaptive Structures papers from structures; 1 Space Exploration paper from exploration), so weight = 26/2814 = 0.00924 and the overall sum is unchanged. It is kept although below the file's 0.02 cutoff. Excluded: aircraft items (thick-origami deployable wing, inflatable wings), entry heatshields/decelerators, solar-sail trajectory papers in Space Flight Mechanics, and a Multi-Layer Plate Deployment mechanism whose application could not be confirmed as space.",
